{"data":{"id":1637,"name":"iExec RLC","symbol":"RLC","slug":"rlc","category":"token","description":"## What Is iExec RLC (RLC)?\n\niExec tools make it easy to build privacy-first applications with programmable governance, data protection, and confidential processing integrated. This allows builders to give users full control of their data and its access, while enabling new models for sharing and monetization.\n\nWe’re creating a world where every transaction, dataset, and application contributes to a safer, more private, and shared economy for users.\n\n**Privacy made easy.**\n\n\n## What Makes iExec RLC Unique?\n\niExec stands apart by offering privacy tools powered by TEEs, making confidential computing simple to integrate for developers. With ready-to-use components like DataProtector and Web3Messaging, builders can add encrypted processing, private communication, and secure data access without managing infrastructure. iExec transforms complex privacy tech into tools that anyone can use to build applications where data ownership and confidentiality are the default.\n\n### How Many iExec RLC (RLC) Are There in Circulation?\n\nIExec RLC (RLC) is a cryptocurrency on the [Ethereum](https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/ethereum/) platform. More specifically, RLC is an[ ERC-20](https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/erc20/) compliant digital asset. \n\nRLC can be easily and securely stored, transferred, traded and divided as well as used to make transactions.\n\n\n### How Is the iExec RLC Secured?\n\nThe iExec network is secured through Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs), which protect computations by keeping data encrypted even while in use. On top of this, the network relies on a Proof-of-Contribution consensus mechanism, ensuring that work completed by providers is validated, verified, and rewarded transparently on-chain.\n\n\n## Who Are the Founders of iExec RLC?\n\nWhen it comes to the Founders of iExec RLC, Gilles Fedak is the CEO and co-founder. Before he began work on iExec, he worked in INRIA as a research scientist at a postdoc in UC San Diego and at ATER at University Paris-Sud. He has a Ph.D. in philosophy and computer science.\n\nHaiwu He is the co-founder and head of APAC at iExec. Before that, he was a professor at the Chinese Academy of Sciences, an innovation transfer research engineer at ENS Lyon, the co-founder of iRentCPU, a research engineer expert at INRA and an assistant professor at Hohai University.  He has a Ph.D. in computing sciences. \n\nThis means that iExec is built upon the work of team members who have done INRIA and CNRS research in the field of desktop grid computing.\n\n\n## Where Can You Buy iExec RLC (RLC)?\n\nWhen it comes to the top exchanges for trading in iExec RLC, these include: \n\n[Bittrex](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/bittrex/)\n\n[Uniswap V2](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/uniswap-v2/)\n\n[Binance](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/binance/)\n\n[Upbit](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/upbit/)\n\n[VCC Exchange](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/vcc-exchange/)\n\n[HitBTC](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/hitbtc/)\n\nFeel free to find more at our crypto[ exchanges page](https://coinmarketcap.com/rankings/exchanges/).\n","dateAdded":"2017-04-20T00:00:00.000Z","actualTimeStart":"2017-04-20T21:45:00.000Z","status":"active","isBn":1,"subStatus":"normal","notice":"","alertType":2,"alertLink":"","latestUpdateTime":"2026-10-19T06:41:00.000Z","watchCount":"86579","watchListRanking":438,"dateLaunched":"2017-04-19T00:00:00.000Z","latestAdded":false,"launchPrice":0.2831,"tags":[{"slug":"marketing","name":"Marketing","category":"INDUSTRY","status":1,"priority":5},{"slug":"art","name":"Art","category":"INDUSTRY","status":1,"priority":5},{"slug":"marketplace","name":"Marketplace","category":"INDUSTRY","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"platform","name":"Platform","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":5},{"slug":"services","name":"Services","category":"INDUSTRY","status":1